#  The melting bracket - the measurement that stands, and the cheap one.
#
#  It needs NO interface-settling stage and NO temperature reading, and it
#  holds ZERO PRESSURE throughout: every stage after the first is NPT.
#  Build a solid half and a liquid half, hold BOTH at a trial temperature,
#  and ask what happened: if the solid melts, Tm is below the trial
#  temperature; if the liquid freezes, Tm is above it; if neither wins, the
#  trial temperature is Tm.  The structure factor per half answers that, and
#  the settling temperature of an interface - the fragile part of the
#  two-phase method, and the part that produced a void 3438 K for tantalum -
#  never enters.  See in.coexistence for that failure and for why each stage
#  below is built the way it is.
#
#  The answer is read from the dumps, never from the thermo output:
#
#      python phase_gate.py *.dump --halves --data perfect.data --a 3.3052
#
#  Measured this way for tantalum's force-matched record (2026-09-22), with a
#  perfect crystal returning S = 1.000 as the control; S of the two halves at
#  the end of a 120 ps hold:
#
#      2000 K   0.760 / 0.802   all solid    the liquid froze   -> Tm > 2000
#      2250 K   0.847 / 0.857   all solid    the liquid froze   -> Tm > 2250
#      2500 K   0.751 / 0.708   all solid    the liquid froze   -> Tm > 2500
#      2750 K   0.068 / 0.098   all liquid   the solid melted   -> Tm < 2750
#
#  so Tm = 2625 +/- 125 K against an experimental 3290 K, 20 per cent low.
#
#  TWO WAYS TO GET A DIFFERENT NUMBER, both of which happened.  A 40 ps hold
#  (NHOLD 20000) is too short: from 2000 to 2500 K neither half had won when it
#  ended, and reading those as "neither wins" gave 2250 +/- 250 K, which the
#  first version of this file reported.  And holding the VOLUME instead of the
#  pressure (nvt in stages B, C and C2) leaves the cell at about 2 GPa near
#  2500 K and raises the apparent melting point; the first published copy of
#  this file did that, while the numbers in its comment came from NPT runs.
#
#  RUN one trial temperature per invocation, in its own directory:
#
#      lmp -in in.coexistence_bracket -var TTRY 2250
#
#  At the midpoint neither half wins inside NHOLD steps, which is what
#  sitting near Tm looks like; do not read that as a failed run.

variable TTRY  index 2250                             # trial temperature, K
variable POT   index potentials/Ta_force_taper.ugur   # potential file
variable EL    index Ta                               # element in that file
variable A0    index 3.3052                           # lattice constant, A
variable MASS  index 180.948                          # atomic mass
variable NX    index 6                                # cells across
variable NZ    index 30                               # cells along z, the long axis
variable TCOLD index 1200                             # where the solid is built
variable THOT  index 6000                             # where the liquid half is melted
variable NEQ   index 20000                            # steps per stage
variable NHOLD index 60000                            # steps of competition at TTRY (120 ps)

units metal
boundary p p p
atom_style atomic

lattice bcc ${A0}
region cell block 0 ${NX} 0 ${NX} 0 ${NZ}
create_box 1 cell
create_atoms 1 box
mass * ${MASS}

pair_style ugur
pair_coeff * * ${POT} ${EL}
neighbor 2.0 bin
timestep 0.002

#  the control the gate needs: a perfect crystal must return S = 1.000
write_data perfect.data nocoeff

variable lz equal "lz"
variable zc equal ${lz}/2
region rliq block INF INF INF INF INF ${zc} units box
group liq region rliq
group sol subtract all liq
compute Tliq liq temp
compute Tsol sol temp

thermo 2500
thermo_style custom step temp pe press vol c_Tliq c_Tsol

#  --- A: the whole cell SOLID, far below the melting point ---------------
velocity all create ${TCOLD} 4928459 mom yes rot yes dist gaussian
fix 1 all npt temp ${TCOLD} ${TCOLD} 0.1 iso 0 0 1.0
run ${NEQ}
unfix 1
write_dump all custom A_solid.dump id type x y z

#  --- B: melt the liquid half only; the solid half is not integrated ------
fix 1 liq npt temp ${THOT} ${THOT} 0.1 z 0 0 2.0
run ${NEQ}
unfix 1
write_dump all custom B_halfmelt.dump id type x y z

#  --- C: bring the liquid half to the trial temperature ------------------
fix 1 liq npt temp ${TTRY} ${TTRY} 0.1 z 0 0 2.0
run ${NEQ}
unfix 1
write_dump all custom C_cooled.dump id type x y z

#  --- C2: hold BOTH halves at the trial temperature.  THIS is the
#  measurement: whichever phase wins says which side of Tm we are on.
fix 1 all npt temp ${TTRY} ${TTRY} 0.1 iso 0 0 2.0
run ${NHOLD}
unfix 1
write_dump all custom C2_both.dump id type x y z
